            <ArticleTitle>[Panarteritis nodosa: infection of the central nervous system with headache and clinical symptoms].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>96-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Headache in various forms is frequent in panarteritis nodosa and possibly is an early symptom of affection of the central nervous system. 2 typical cases are described. In up to 13% of patients with panarteritis nodosa the central nervous system is affected, the forms of the disease are described as well as development of prognosis under today's therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
